%description:

Tcp.swsOverrideAfterRto:linux -- the override timeout of the sender SWS avoidance is one RTO, also above 1.0 s.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "true: one RTO, at most maxPersistTimeout, as Linux, which sends such data from its probe timer
(tcp_probe_timer(), tcp_write_wakeup())".

The classes: rfc-upper and rfc-lower (false): the RTO held in the range 0.1 s to 1.0 s of RFC 9293 section 3.8.6.2.1;
linux (true; the value of LinuxTcp): one RTO. The code: TcpAlgorithmBase::startPersistTimer() and
processPersistTimer(). This test separates "linux" from "rfc-upper".

Host under test: host1, with an MSS of 1000 bytes and a minimum RTO of 2 s, so its RTO is 2 s, sends 5000 bytes. The
TS option takes 12 bytes of each segment, so a full segment holds 988 bytes. Peer: host2, with an advertised window of
3464 bytes, reads nothing. After three segments, 2964 bytes, the window of host2 is 500 bytes, and host1 holds the
rest. Observation: level 1, host1 sends no data for 1.9 s after the hold, and sends the held data 2 s after the hold.

%# parameter: Tcp.swsOverrideAfterRto
%# class: linux
%# value: true
%# key: *.host1.tcp.swsOverrideAfterRto
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpSwsOverrideAfterRtoLinux")
        .act(action().at(0.0).run<TcpTestApp>("host2.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) {
            app.socket().setAutoRead(false);
            app.socket().bind(1000);
            app.socket().listen();
        }))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.ackBit == true && tcp.window == 500")
             .describe("the ACK of host2 that leaves a window of 500 bytes: host1 holds its data")
             .within(1.0))
        .never(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
              .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
              .describe("held data before one RTO, 2 s, after the hold")
              .within(1.9))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
             .describe("the held data, one RTO after the hold")
             .within(0.2));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpSwsOverrideAfterRtoLinux compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.swsOverrideAfterRto = true    # the parameter under test
**.tcp.mss = 1000
*.host1.tcp.minRexmitTimeout = 2s
*.host2.tcp.advertisedWindow = 3464
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 5000B
*.host2.app[0].typename = "TcpTestApp"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpSwsOverrideAfterRtoLinux: PASS
